source: tests/cli.rs
expression: help.assert_exit_code(0).stdout()
---
Compile Lisp source files to Rust

Usage: knave [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  check   Read, expand and check a program, then print its diagnostics
  types   Print the inferred signature of each function in a program
  doc     Print the page of a prelude term, or of a program's term with --file
  expand  Print a program as kernel forms after macro expansion
  emit    Print the Rust code generated for a program
  fmt     Lay out source files in place, or standard input given `-`
  build   Compile a program to a native binary
  eval    Check a module, then run forms once in its scope and print their values
  repl    Read forms at a prompt, keep the definitions and run the rest
  test    Build the tests of a file or a directory and run them
  run     Build a program and run it
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --color <WHEN>  When to color the output [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help          Print help
  -V, --version       Print version

With no command, start the prompt as repl does.
